<title>USA: U.S. crop progress highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. crop progress highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture said Monday that 73 percent of the U.S. soybean crop had been harvested, compared to 63 percent a week ago and a ive-year average of 81 percent.</p>
<p>In its report on Oct. 27 conditions, USDA said 45 percent of corn was harvested. A week earlier, 30 percent had been harvested, and the five-year average is 60 percent.</p>
<p>USDA said 53 percent of the cotton crop was harvested versus 45 percent last week, and 54 percent average.</p>
<p>USDA said 90 percent of the winter wheat crop had been planted, versus 85 percent a week ago and 88 percent average. It said 74 percent of the crop had emerged, compared to 63 percent a week ago and 70 percent average.</p>
<p>The department also reported three percent of the winter wheat crop was in poor condition, 26 percent fair, 58 percent good and 13 percent excellent.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8394</p>
</text>
